<!--
  Still a single URL, not one entry per example — but NOT for the
  reason a stale version of this comment used to give. This app now
  uses plain HTML5 path-based routing (main.ts, no withHashLocation()),
  so every /examples/NN-slug route IS a real, distinct URL a crawler
  can request directly (unlike a hash fragment, which never reaches
  the server at all) — that part of the old reasoning no longer holds.
  What's still true: this is a client-rendered SPA with no per-route
  <title>/meta tags of its own (confirmed directly against
  src/index.html — canonical/OG/Twitter are all static, app-wide
  values, not swapped per route), so every one of those 53 URLs would
  serve identical metadata if listed here; the real per-example
  content (titles, descriptions) is indexed instead through astro-
  docs' own docs pages, which link out to each specific example route
  (see astro.config.mjs's own Angular Examples sidebar section there).
  Worth revisiting if this app ever adds real per-route metadata via
  Angular's Title/Meta services — at that point listing all 53 URLs
  here would become genuinely more indexable, not just longer.
-->
